# CPP — Feed-Level Spark Transformation Timeout Implementation

## Role

Act as a Senior Scala, Apache Spark, and Distributed Systems Engineer working on an existing enterprise reconciliation application.

You have access to the CPP source code through IntelliJ.

Your responsibility is to implement, test, and validate **feed-level Spark transformation timeout handling** while preserving existing application behavior.

This is an implementation task, not just a design exercise.

Do not deploy or merge changes.

## 1. Existing architecture

The Core PreProcessor (CPP) application runs on Apache Spark using Scala.

Current execution behavior:

- One CPP Spark application processes multiple input feeds.
- Input files are available in the configured CPP processing path on HDFS.
- The Spark driver uses a Scala ForkJoin pool.
- The configured parallelism is 10 concurrent feed-processing tasks.
- Each worker independently processes a feed.
- When a worker completes, it becomes available for another queued feed.
- Different feeds can submit Spark actions concurrently.
- All feeds share the same SparkContext and Spark executor resources.
- Current source investigation found no implementation of `setJobGroup`, `cancelJobGroup`, or `clearJobGroup`.
- Existing audit logging, file archive, and failure-handling mechanisms are already implemented.

Do not introduce another Spark application or replace the ForkJoin execution model.

## 2. Business requirement

Introduce a **configurable 30-minute timeout for the transformation phase of each feed**.

The timeout must NOT apply to the entire CPP execution lifecycle.

For example:

| Operation | Duration | Timeout applicability |
|---|---|---|
| Read and initialize feed | 5 minutes | Excluded |
| Execute transformation | 28 minutes | Included |
| Write output | 2 minutes | Excluded, where separately measurable |
| Archive and update audit | 1 minute | Excluded |

This feed must complete successfully because its transformation took only 28 minutes.

If the transformation itself reaches 30 minutes without completing, CPP must stop the associated Spark work and execute the existing failure-handling lifecycle.

The requirement applies to the existing CPP transformation path. Do not change CPP-versus-AI gating logic or any unreleased transformation-count feature.

